From 4c7f91927e86b91f7522209dbda1f1f779b445fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:11:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: octagon: use device-mode HS PHY init value
 0x00d1d9a4

What was wrong: the HS PHY parameter-override value programmed for the
gadget (device) mode was 0x00d191a4. That is the value the original Lumia
kernel uses for HOST mode only. For device mode it uses 0x00d1d9a4
(differs in bits 14 and 11, PHY tuning).

Source: Android4Lumia950/android_kernel_mmo_msm8994 (branch
lineage-18.1-talkman), arch/arm64/boot/dts/mmo/msm8994-chi.dtsi:

    &hsphy0 {
        qcom,hsphy-init-host = <0x00D191A4>;
        qcom,hsphy-init      = <0x00D1D9A4>;   /* device mode */
    };

The same file also shows that the original kernel runs the USB gadget on
DWC3 + hsphy0 (f92f8800/f9b3a000) and disables the QUSB2/ChipIdea PHY, so
the DWC3 path is the right one for the Type-C data lines; the ChipIdea
experiments (cityman-safe-ci) were a detour. The HS PHY init sequence in
drivers/usb/phy/phy-msm-hsusb.c of that tree matches our
phy-msm8994-hsusb.c (sleep-clk reset, HS_PHY_CTRL, COMMON, override).

Signed-off-by: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
index 7949f2c1b3b..70610f26411 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon.dtsi
@@ -792,7 +792,7 @@ &usb3_hsphy {
 
 	vdda18-supply = <&vreg_l6a_1p8>;
 	vdda33-supply = <&vreg_l24a_3p075>;
-	qcom,hsphy-init = <0x00d191a4>;
+	qcom,hsphy-init = <0x00d1d9a4>;
 	qcom,set-pllbtune;
 };
 
